        "created_at": "2014-04-04T11:05:44.000Z",
        "cooked": "<h4><strong>Intro</strong></h4>#NEWLINE#To recognize the folks who have done so much to promote the Greater Than Games community, we've created a set of annual forum awards! The award descriptions, nomination rules, and voting rules are below. These rules are to make sure the process is as fair, simple, and easy-to-run as possible.#NEWLINE##NEWLINE#[color=red]<em>Please do not post in this thread - see below for how this thread will be used.</em>[/color] We've also created <a href=\"https://greaterthangames.com/forum/topic/forum-awards-discussions-2013-5137\">a discussion thread </a>for the awards and process, but that thread will remain focused on those topics - no campaigning / advertising (see below).#NEWLINE##NEWLINE#(The timing on this is aimed primarily to work around International TableTop Day and PAX East, so everyone involved can do what needs to be done.)#NEWLINE#<h4>Awards</h4>#NEWLINE#In all cases, \"the past year\" is 1-Apr-2013 to 31-Mar-2014. The winners of the awards will receive the community's recognition and thanks, plus special forum badges to show the award they've won.#NEWLINE#<ol>\n<li>\n<em>Inspiring Presence </em>(Morale Booster) – The forum member who, through positive attitude and kind heart, did the most to make the Greater Than Games forums a positive experience over the past year</li>\n<li>\n<em>Bolster Allies </em>(Funniest) – The forum member who was best at making people laugh and providing humorous moments over the past year</li>\n<li>\n<em>Truth Seeker </em>(Lore Master) – The forum member who has done the best job answering questions (rules, facts, mythology, etc.) and otherwise providing useful and accurate information over the past year</li>\n<li>\n<em>Harmony </em>(Top Debater) – The forum member who is best at rationally debating positions (without turning it into a fight) over the past year</li>\n<li>\n<em>Exceeded Expectations </em>(Top Contributor) – The forum member who contributed to the Greater Than Games community with tools and/or accessories the most over the past year</li>\n<li>\n<em>Bring What You Need </em>(Top Wikier) – The forum member who contributed most to the Greater Than Games wikis over the past year</li>\n<li>\n<em>Unique Capabilities </em>(Top Artist) – The forum member who created the best/most Greater Than Games-related art or fanfic over the past year</li>\n</ol>#NEWLINE#&nbsp;#NEWLINE##NEWLINE#And here's what the awesome forum badges for the award winners will look like:#NEWLINE##NEWLINE#![](upload://hjCECp8BEy4m6Q9Nf3yo8kwwJS5.png)<br><span alt=\"\" class=\"broken-image\" title=\"This image is broken\"><svg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-unlink svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use xlink:href=\"#unlink\"></use></svg></span><br><span alt=\"\" class=\"broken-image\" title=\"This image is broken\"><svg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-unlink svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use xlink:href=\"#unlink\"></use></svg></span><br><span alt=\"\" class=\"broken-image\" title=\"This image is broken\"><svg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-unlink svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use xlink:href=\"#unlink\"></use></svg></span><br><span alt=\"\" class=\"broken-image\" title=\"This image is broken\"><svg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-unlink svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use xlink:href=\"#unlink\"></use></svg></span><br><span alt=\"\" class=\"broken-image\" title=\"This image is broken\"><svg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-unlink svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use xlink:href=\"#unlink\"></use></svg></span><br><span alt=\"\" class=\"broken-image\" title=\"This image is broken\"><svg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-unlink svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use xlink:href=\"#unlink\"></use></svg></span>#NEWLINE##NEWLINE#&nbsp;#NEWLINE#<h4>Rules for Nominations</h4><ul>\n<li>Nomination is recognition of a forum member's impact in the category; a nomination shows the nominator feels the forum member has significantly contributed in the category.</li>\n<li>These rules are to help ensure we don't miss anyone in the process of collecting the nominations - we really don't want to do that!</li>\n<li>Nominations will be sent as a Personal Message to one (and only one) of the Moderators: arenson9, imprimis, or Rabit.</li>\n<li>The nominations will be listed in this thread - the moderators will add them as they process them.</li>\n<li>Nominations made between noon on <strong>7-Apr </strong>and noon <strong>14-Apr</strong>, EST, will be counted for nomination.</li>\n<li>Each nomination should be a list of the awards and the nominee(s). For example (and feel free to copy-and-paste this):<br><em>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Inspiring Presence </em>- ForumMember1<br><em><em>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </em>Bolster Allies </em>- ForumMember2<br><em><em>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </em>Truth Seeker </em>- ForumMember3<br><em><em>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </em>Harmony </em>- ForumMember4<br><em><em>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </em>Exceeded Expectations </em><em>- </em>ForumMember5<br><em><em>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </em>Bring What You Need </em>- ForumMember6<br><em><em>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </em>Unique Capabilities </em>- ForumMember7</li>\n</ul><ul>\n<li>A nomination needs to be the names of awards with nominated forum members names and a short blurb describing why the forum member deserves to receive the award.</li>\n<li>A nomination does not have to include all awards; you can include any number of awards in your nomination post.</li>\n<li>If a forum member has already been nominated, don't nominate them again – repeated nominations will be ignored.</li>\n<li>Admins and Mods cannot be nominated – nominations for Admins and Mods will be deleted.</li>\n<li>[color=green]No campaigning, advertising, or otherwise promoting a nomination is allowed (anywhere on the forum) – the awards are to be based on proven activity over the past year and nothing else.[/color]</li>\n</ul>#NEWLINE#&nbsp;#NEWLINE#<h4>Rules for Voting</h4><ul>\n<li>On 15-Apr, there will be a post in this thread with a link to the survey for voting.</li>\n<li>Voting will occur between noon on <strong>15-Apr </strong>and noon <strong>21-Apr</strong>, EST.</li>\n<li>Each forum member will get one vote for each award.</li>\n<li>\n<strong>You may now vote here:&nbsp;</strong> https://www.surveymonkey.com/s/RCRG7GY </li>\n</ul>#NEWLINE#&nbsp;#NEWLINE#",
